---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Matt Kilcoyne - Policy analyst, economist, and builder of coordination infrastructure">
  <article class="about">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <section>
      <p>
        Matt Kilcoyne. Policy analyst at the
        <a href="https://datainnovation.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Center for Data Innovation</a>
        and <a href="https://itif.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ITIF</a>.
        Based in London.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work at the intersection of economics, technology policy, and coordination mechanisms.
        My focus is on how institutions shape outcomes, how technology changes what's possible,
        and how we build infrastructure for collective action without capture.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Background</h2>
      <p>
        Previously at the Adam Smith Institute and the Open Data Institute.
        My policy work has contributed to UK government decisions on trade, regulation, and
        digital infrastructure.
      </p>
      <p>
        Current research areas include the economics of AI governance,
        European digital sovereignty critique, and formalizing LLMs as navigation tools
        through possibility space (the Babel Navigation Theorem).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Approach</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Follow the money</strong> &mdash; Track distributional effects and rent-seeking to understand policy</li>
        <li><strong>Navigation beats prediction</strong> &mdash; Explore possibility space rather than forecast complex systems</li>
        <li><strong>Build coordination infrastructure</strong> &mdash; Enable collective action without capture</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Projects</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/brunel">The Brunel Engine</a> &mdash; A structured interview tool that generates private reports
        to help users turn frustrations into actionable insights. The entry point to a broader
        ecosystem of coordination tools.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul class="contact-list">
        <li><a href="https://twitter.com/MattKilcoyne" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Twitter/X: @MattKilcoyne</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://datainnovation.org/author/mkilcoyne/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Professional work at CDI</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding: 2rem 0;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: #58a6ff;
  }

  section {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: #c9d1d9;
  }

  p {
    margin: 1rem 0;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  a {
    color: #58a6ff;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  ul {
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  li {
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .contact-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin-left: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
